# Open Design

This repository is wired for [Open Design](https://open-design.ai/) (nexu-io/open-design).

When the user asks for design, UI, prototypes, decks, or visual direction:

1. Read `DESIGN.md` and `design-systems/typing-trainer/tokens.css` first.
2. Follow the matching skill under `skills/` (start with `frontend-design`; use `taste-skill` if the look feels generic).
3. Prefer real artifacts: self-contained HTML under `artifacts/open-design/` or production code in the app framework.
4. Use CSS variables from `tokens.css`. Do not invent palette hex values.
5. If the Open Design daemon is reachable (`http://127.0.0.1:7456`), create/update project `typing-trainer2`, attach design system `typing-trainer`, and save generated HTML into the project via the API or MCP tools.
6. Avoid AI-default aesthetics called out in `DESIGN.md` (purple gradients, Inter-as-display, hero cards, pill clusters).

Daemon helpers:

- Health: `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:7456/api/health`
- Start locally: `./scripts/od-start.sh`
